Acceptance and object-store accounting

deploy/metal/e2e.sh on the vhost-user block path with real S3, this branch:

  metal e2e: 22 passed, 1 failed

The one failure is the same stale assertion PR #8 already recorded -- the golden
rootfs has apt and curl but no git -- and is unrelated to the block path or to
these changes. So delta packs and golden roots leave the acceptance score exactly
where it was.

In the bucket at the end of the session, under the node's `e2e/` prefix:

  e2e/images/    74 objects   306 MB   <- the rootfs, published once
  e2e/volumes/   43 volumes            <- every Cat created during the session

74 objects is the whole 512 MiB rootfs after dropping its all-zero chunks, stored
once and referenced by every Cat that started from it. Before this change each of
those 43 volumes would have carried its own copy.

(The volumes/ byte total is not a clean number for this comparison: the session
ran both builds against the same bucket, so most of those bytes are the copy-path
baseline runs.)
